From aff20fcbfde24ef8a1b512dacdbb2517579e30e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g1-door <g1-door@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:33:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] door: optional clearance penalty to the door frame covers and
 the walls with an adaptive weight (env.config.wall_gap: for the fingertip,
 palm, wrist, forearm middle and elbow of both arms, the fingertip being the
 palm plus tip_m along wrist to palm as in the real forward kinematics, the
 top view signed distance to the cover boxes from the opening edge over the
 cover width and to the wall boxes beyond, on both sides, gives a cost of the
 sum of max(0, x_m - d) / x_m, so that passing close is penalised before
 touching; rewards.reward_scales.wall_gap_lagrange=1.0 returns minus lambda
 times the cost, and at every episode end the episodes that came within x_m
 once count as violations, whose rate as an exponential moving average moves
 lambda up while above target_rate and down otherwise between 0 and
 lambda_max, kept in state_path across chain rounds and not updated while
 evaluating; the door customData now carries coverWidth, coverFrontX,
 wallFrontX and gapWidth; x_m 0.06 since on 11-11 the real hand touched the
 frame and the wall in two runs while the model points were 3.3 to 4.5 cm
 away, plus about 1 cm left after correcting stage 0 with the point cloud
 (user, option 2); default off = unchanged) (11-11)

